WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.560
Television screen, an envelope

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.880
or a canvas are all examples of quadrilateral.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.640
Quadrilateral is one word,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.680
but you can see that this part is coloured red,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.460
and this part is coloured blue.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.080
'Quadri' basically means 'four'

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.900
and 'lateral' means 'sides'.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.120
If you observe, all these things have four sides.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.180
This is an example of a quadrilateral.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.080
To name the quadrilateral, we give names to these four points.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.200
We call them A,B,C and D.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.060
These things that we just named are called vertices.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:49.040
And the quadrilateral will always have four vertices.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.780
Each point is called the vertex.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.320
And as we've already seen a quadrilateral has four sides.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:02.160
And the sides are called AB, BC, CD and DA.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.120
So remember, every quadrilateral has four sides and four vertices.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.140
There's an another important property of quadrilaterals.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.000
Consider this table.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.500
The surface of this table is flat,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.460
It's a plain surface.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:24.100
If I draw a quadrilateral on a table, it will look something like this.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.660
If you look at the quadrilateral closely,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.580
you can see that all the vertices

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.740
and sides of the quadrilateral

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.120
lie on one plane.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.060
So a quadrilateral has four sides,

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.940
four vertices and is a closed figure lying on one plane.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.040
Observe that a vertex is formed when two sides meet at a point.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.240
And what is formed between those sides is called an angle.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.800
This is an angle.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.640
A quadrilateral is also defined by its angles.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.800
It has four angles.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:05.600
Apart from the one we marked this one, this one and this one.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.460
These are the four angles formed in a quadrilateral.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.920
But how do we name the angles?

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.680
How can we name this green angle?

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.980
Well, we can call it angle A.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.920
We just named the angle based on the vertex at which it is formed.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.880
But a better way to name it is to call it angle DAB.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.100
Or you can also call it angle BAD.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.180
In these two cases, we named it based on the sides.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.180
Similarly, this angle can be called angle ABC.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.340
This one can be called angle BCD.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:46.940
And this one angle CDA.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.660
And here's the last basic concept you need to know.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.720
In this quadrilateral,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.580
vertices A and C are opposite to each other.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.200
And vertices B and D are opposite to each other.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.860
The lines joining the opposite vertices

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.200
are called the diagonals of the quadrilateral.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.940
So these two lines are called the diagonals.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:17.220
In this figure we can say that AC and BD are the diagonals.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.040
What are its practical applications?

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.840
When you watch this video on a 17 inch laptop,

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.520
what you think is 17 inches?

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.200
It's the length of the diagonal.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.520
Even when you watch your favorite TV series on a 51 inch TV,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.620
it's the diagonal that is 51 inches.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.080
So remember,

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.060
a quadrilateral is a closed figure on one plane which has four sides,

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.040
four vertices and four angles.

